Determine the correct result here. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {6, 3, 2, -4, 3, 7, -3, -3};
int acc = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) if (a[i] > 2) acc++;
return acc;

Here is an exam-style problem. What does this string routine return?
String s = "xeoeiyc";
int acc = 0, target = 'u';
for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) if (s.charAt(i) == target) acc++;
return acc;

Here is an exam-style problem. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {0, 4, 5, 9, 10, 11, 15};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 26) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 26) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

Choose the best answer to this. What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(5);
Node b = new Node(20);
Node c = new Node(30);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

Decide which option is correct. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {4, 7, 12, 13, 15, 16, 19, 20, 24, 26, 28};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 26) return mid; if (a[mid] < 26) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return -1;

Here is an exam-style problem. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {1, 1, 0, -3, 1, -1, 2, -3};
int acc = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) acc += a[i];
return acc;

Reason from first principles here. What does this string routine return?
